   "datePublished": "2026-11-16T18:39:49.515+00:00",
   "description": "Reproduction of the solar-capture test of inelastic dark matter after the 248 keV LZ nuclear-recoil candidate (Di Mauro & Shaikh 2026, arXiv:2609.06760; paper 09_Solar_Capture_Inelastic_DM_LZ.pdf in papers/). Uses the project's physics engine (tools/physics.py) to (a) model the endothermic solar-capture rate vs. mass splitting δ, (b) evaluate IceCube annihilation-rate limits in three post-capture cooling scenarios, (c) show the mixed-DM (WIMP + sterile-ν) χ² constraint plane after Higgsino exclusion, and (d) overlay BBN Y_p/D/H predictions vs. N_eff for three scenarios. Scripts live in analysis/; figures are committed to analysis/output/ (the repo's .gitignore excludes *.png elsewhere but explicitly re-includes analysis/output/*.png).",
